From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 19:55:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] metainfo-cache: No AppStream pool without GNOME Software

The cache serves only the uninstall action of the app grid, and that
action is offered only when gnome-software is installed. Still the pool
was created at startup with the OS catalog, all Flatpak remotes and
AS_POOL_FLAG_MONITOR.

Every change of the AppStream data (a Flatpak appstream refresh, a
package installing desktop or metainfo files) reloads the whole catalog.
On a phone with Flathub configured each reload left about 60 MB in malloc
arenas of the shell: after a few updates Phosh held about 1 GB.

Without gnome-software the pool is not created at all and
phosh_metainfo_get_data_id () returns NULL.
---
 src/metainfo-cache.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/metainfo-cache.c b/src/metainfo-cache.c
index 7c494da5..71791736 100644
--- a/src/metainfo-cache.c
+++ b/src/metainfo-cache.c
@@ -88,6 +88,15 @@ phosh_metainfo_cache_constructed (GObject *object)
 
   G_OBJECT_CLASS (phosh_metainfo_cache_parent_class)->constructed (object);
 
+  /* Only the uninstall action of the app grid uses the cache and it needs
+   * GNOME Software. Without it the pool would load the whole catalog of
+   * every Flatpak remote and reload it on each change of the AppStream
+   * data, keeping hundreds of MB in the shell for nothing. */
+  if (!phosh_util_have_gnome_software (FALSE)) {
+    g_debug ("No GNOME Software, not loading the metainfo pool");
+    return;
+  }
+
   self->as_pool = as_pool_new ();
   /* We only bother about metainfo in a non-system cache */
   as_pool_set_flags (self->as_pool,
@@ -189,6 +198,10 @@ phosh_metainfo_get_data_id (PhoshMetainfoCache *self, const char *app_id)
 {
   g_autoptr (AsComponentBox) result = NULL;
 
+  /* No pool without GNOME Software, see constructed () */
+  if (!self->as_pool)
+    return NULL;
+
   result = as_pool_get_components_by_launchable (self->as_pool, AS_LAUNCHABLE_KIND_DESKTOP_ID,
                                                  app_id);
 
